                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/topos+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#categories_of_small_presheaves"} Categories of small presheaves
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong small presheaf
            on a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            which is determined by a small amount of data. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is itself
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is small, but this is no longer true when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is large. In many cases, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is large, it is the small presheaves which seem to be more important and useful.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            which is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C^{op}\to Set
            is
            %strong small
            if it is the left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            of some functor whose domain is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representable functors
            (see Proposition 4.83 of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Kelly82"} Kelly
          %p
            Of course, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is itself small, then every presheaf is small.
          %h2#categories_of_small_presheaves Categories of small presheaves
          %p
            We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
            for the category of small presheaves on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em all
            presheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            cannot be defined without the assumption of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+universe"} universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
            can be so defined, using small diagrams in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as proxies for small colimits of representable presheaves. Moreover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
            is locally small, and there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\hookrightarrow P C
          %p
            Of course, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is small, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
            is the usual category of all presheaves on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Since small colimits of small colimits are small colimits,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is not small. It is not, in general, complete, but we can characterize when it is (cf. Day–Lack).
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
              is complete if and only if for every small diagram in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .un_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is either complete or small, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C
              is complete.
          %p We also have:
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              are complete, then a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to D
              preserves small limits if and only if the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P F\colon P C \to P D
              (induced by left Kan extension) also preserves small limits.
          %p
            These results can all be generalized to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            (which, for some purposes, we might want to assume to be “saturated”). See the paper by Day and Lack.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Kelly82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Basic concepts of enriched category theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 64
                %strong 10
                (2005) 1-136 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/de/academic/subjects/mathematics/logic-categories-and-sets/basic-concepts-enriched-category-theory?format=PB&isbn=9780521287029"}> ISBN:9780521287029
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10abs.html"} tac:tr10
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+J.+Day"}> Brian J. Day
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"} Stephen Lack
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Limits of small functors
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2006.10.019"} doi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0610439"} arXiv
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.usyd.edu.au/u/stevel/papers/small.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Chorny"}> Boris Chorny
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"} William Dwyer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The homotopy theory of small diagrams over large categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/forum.2009.009"} doi
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0607117"} arXiv
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"}> Paolo Perrone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kan extensions are partial colimits
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.04531"} arXiv:2101.04531
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-021-09671-9"} doi
          %p The results of Chorny–Dwyer are cited by Rosický in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"}> Jiří Rosický
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Accessible categories and homotopy theory
              %a{:href => "https://www.math.muni.cz/~rosicky/papers/homacc3.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Biedermann"}> Georg Biedermann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Chorny"} Boris Chorny
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality and small functors
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2015.15.2609"} doi
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Chorny"}> Boris Chorny
                , David White,
                %em A variant of a Dwyer-Kan theorem for model categories
                (v1:
                = succeed ")," do
                  %em Homotopy theory of homotopy presheaves
                = succeed ":4," do
                  %strong 24
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.05378"} arXiv:1805.05378
          %p
            On when
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+continuous"} finitely continuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            are small:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Ad%C3%A1mek"}> Jiří Adámek
              , V. Koubek, and V. Trnková.
              = succeed "." do
                %em How large are left exact functors?
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/8/n13/n13.pdf"} pdf
